  "scope": "Every continuous f:R^m to R^n has the printed countable Borel cover of its actual surjective-differential locus. Each piece carries p in O*(m,m-n), two globally Lipschitz maps u,v, and the exact laws u(x)=(f(x),p(x)), v(u(x))=x. All natural dimensions are covered, including empty full-rank locus for m<n and both zero-dimensional blocks. The proof follows the finite coordinate family, 1.7.4 kernel separation, 3.2.2 and sealed Kirszbraun extension.",
